## Data (`data/`, `dist/`)

The compiled administrative dataset is a fusion of the following sources:

### 1. Administrative structure, P-codes, polygons, areas, centroids, capitals

Source: **OCHA COD-AB — "Mauritania - Subnational Administrative Boundaries"**
<https://data.humdata.org/dataset/cod-ab-mrt> (dataset version of January 2026).

- License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY 4.0)
- © United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA),
  derived from official Mauritanian administrative sources.
- Portions of the underlying geometry may originate from OpenStreetMap and are
  © OpenStreetMap contributors under the Open Database License (ODbL 1.0)
  <https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/>.

Known deviations we deliberately corrected (documented for transparency):

- OCHA lists commune `Teyaret` under moughataa `Toujounine` and commune
  `Toujounine` under moughataa `Teyarett`. French and English Wikipedia
  ("Departments of Mauritania") confirm each commune belongs to the
  same-named moughataa; `mauritania-geo` applies this fix.
- Commune P-codes of the three Nouakchott wilayas in the OCHA file follow a
  legacy scheme (`MR013xx`); `mauritania-geo` therefore assigns its own stable
  6-digit codes (see README §Identifiers) and keeps the OCHA P-code in
  `p_code` for traceability.
- The moughataa OCHA calls `Lexeibe 1` is written `Lexeiba 1` following
  French Wikipedia / citypopulation.de; both forms are searchable.

### 2. ISO 3166-2 codes

Source: ISO 3166-2:MR (ISO 3166 Maintenance Agency — Online Browsing Platform,
<https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:code:3166:MR>). ISO country/region codes are
facts and not copyrightable; the list was cross-checked against
en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-2:MR and fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-2:MR.
MR-13/14/15 (Nouakchott-Ouest/Nord/Sud) were added and MR-NKC deleted by the
ISO newsletter of 27 November 2015.

### 3. French canonical spellings

Cross-checked between French Wikipedia (CC-BY-SA 4.0) and
<https://www.citypopulation.de/en/mauritania/> (Thomas Brinkhoff, fair-use
reference). Where the two agreed on a different transliteration than OCHA's,
the Wikipedia/citypopulation spelling is used and the OCHA spelling is kept
as a searchable alias.

### 4. Arabic names

From Arabic Wikipedia (CC-BY-SA 4.0): the 15 wilaya articles
(ولاية الحوض الشرقي, ولاية العصابة, …), مقاطعات موريتانيا and per-moughataa
commune lists. Arabic names are missing for 1 moughataa (Touil) and 56
communes (mostly post-2018/2021 creations without Arabic Wikipedia articles);
these carry `name_ar: null` and are marked in `dist/meta.json`.

